{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>For I will drive out.</b> Its meaning is explained in this passage [as to] why [the word] כי was not mentioned the first time, because there was no need: since HaShem commanded that all male Israelites go up to see His face, there is no doubt that HaShem will guard their land from the enemy, since all Israel do His will. And this reason He explained well." "<b>And the sense of \"no man shall covet your land.\"</b> So much will I send terror into the hearts of the neighbors that they will not even covet the land, even if it enters their heart to make war."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:23.893909749Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}